arm64-darwin  a definition cxx1 emits and clang emits only for a use - an inline function or special member (C1/D1 beside C2/D2), a template instance, an unused internal constant or exit helper: emission, not spelling (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "Weak definitions, and the link that follows from them"; tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names"); and clang 19 spells a non-type parameter of dependent type TnT_/TpTn, which cxx1, cl and earlier clangs do not (tests/open/names-register.txt, "Clang 19, not cxx1") - 8 names, e.g. <__Z6seqSumIcJLc97ELc1EEEi3SeqIT_JXspT0_EEE <__Z6seqSumIiJLi4ELi5EEEi3SeqIT_JXspT0_EEE (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
